3,Gadsup language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/gadsup_language,"Gadsup is a Trans–New Guinea language spoken by approximately 22,000 people primarily in the Kainantu district of Eastern Highlands Province and parts of Morobe Province, Papua New Guinea. [1] [2] It belongs to the Kainantu-Goroka subgroup of the East New Guinea Highlands stock, within the broader Papuan language family, and is classified under the Gauwa branch alongside related languages ...",Gadsup,Trans-New Guinea
